# Dev uses the LOCAL audio files in public/quest-audio (vite serves them at
# /quest-audio). Do NOT point dev at R2: files not yet uploaded there (e.g. a
# new language mid-rollout) 404 and fall back to live TTS, which synthesizes
# a different take on every play — the "different audio tracks" bug.
# Production gets the R2 URL at build time:
#   VITE_AUDIO_BASE_URL=https://pub-fa9d7e83944246fcb9a03f217e1dd0c9.r2.dev/quest-audio npm run build

# ─── Analytics (PostHog) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Analytics is DISABLED whenever VITE_POSTHOG_KEY is unset — every capture is
# a silent no-op, which is the intended default for local development.
#
# NEVER commit a real key. This file is git-tracked; put real values in
# `.env.local` (gitignored) instead, or export them in your shell:
#   VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxx            # PostHog project API key
#   VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com   # optional; defaults to US cloud
#
# Full event catalogue + privacy rules: docs/analytics-tracking-plan.md
# Runtime kill switches (opt-out, etc.): src/services/analyticsService.ts
